    {
      "Component": "Training strategy",
      "Name": "Perform training",
      "Title": "Training",
      "Id": "frAQBc",
      "Subtasks": [
        {
          "Type": "Description",
          "Title": "Training",
          "Id": "8Wsa1x",
          "Caption": {
            "Id": "VPfvJc",
            "Content": "Description"
          },
          "Text": "The procedure used to carry out the learning process is called the training strategy.\nIt is applied to the neural network to minimize the loss.\nThe training method is determined by how the neural network parameters are adjusted."
        },
        {
          "Type": "Text",
          "Title": "Optimization algorithm",
          "Id": "rgRYwT",
          "Content": "The quasi-Newton method is used here for training.\nIt is based on Newton's method but does not require the calculation of second derivatives.\nInstead, the quasi-Newton method computes an approximation of the inverse Hessian at each iteration of the algorithm using only gradient information."
        },
        {
          "Type": "DoubleLineChart",
          "Title": "Quasi-Newton method error history",
          "Id": "iizs2t",
          "Caption": {
            "Id": "rQF69A",
            "Content": "The following plot shows the training and validation errors at each epoch.\nThe blue line represents the training error, and the red line represents the validation error.\nThe initial training error is 0.0491, and its final value after 500 epochs is 0.0491.\nThe initial validation error is 0.061, and its final value after 500 epochs is 0.0611.\n"
          },
