        {
          "Type": "Text",
          "Title": "Discussion",
          "Id": "hm3soL",
          "Content": "Training error measures model performance on the data used for training, while validation error measures performance on data not used for training.\nThe goal of a machine learning model is to achieve low validation error and generalize well to new data rather than simply memorizing the training data."
        }
