          "Id": "8Wsa1x",
          "Caption": {
            "Id": "VPfvJc",
            "Content": "Description"
          },
          "Text": "The goodness-of-fit of a model describes how well its predictions match a set of observations. This analysis is performed on the testing subset, which was not used during training.\nThe most common goodness-of-fit measure is the coefficient of determination (R2), computed here as the squared linear correlation between the predicted and the actual values.\nR2 ranges from 0 to 1: a value of 1 means that predicted and actual values are perfectly linearly related, and a value of 0 means that the model explains none of the variation of the target.\n"
        },
